        skos:altLabel          "BAS Sonic sonobuoy";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/369/>;
        skos:definition        "A British Antarctic Survey-built prototype of a free-floating re-usable sonobuoy, designed to record low frequency acoustic information generated by remote marine seismic sources. The instrument is used in conjunction with a towed airgun array, or other remote marine seismic sources. Further details can be found in section 10.10 of JR18 cruise report."@en;
