        skos:definition        "An optical scattering meter designed to measure in situ turbidity in various marine environments. The (S) in the designation signifies the capability of the NTU with an integrated anti-fouling Bio-Wiper. The instrument measures turbidity at a wavelenth of 700 nm over the range 0-125 NTU (nephelometric turbidity units), with a sensitivity of 0.02 NTU, or a range of 0-1000 NTU at a sensitivity of 0.12 NTU. The (S) instrument is stable over a temperature range of 0-30 degC. and is depth-rated to 300 m."@en;
