        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "NMFSS Single-Channel Airgun";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/369/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/153/>;
        skos:definition        "A NMFSS-built single-channel seismic reflection profiling system. The system uses a Bolt 1500C airgun as sound source, and a short hydrophone streamer."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL1198";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "National Marine Facilities Sea Systems (NMFSS) Single-Channel Airgun Seismic Reflection System"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00125/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0849/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL0849";
        dc:date                "2016-11-09 16:50:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL0849";
        pav:authoredOn         "2016-11-09 16:50:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0849/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0849/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "Shimadzu TOC-VCPH";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/LAB01/>;
        skos:definition        "A PC-controlled, total organic carbon analyser (high-sensitivity model), designed to measure total carbon (TC), inorganic carbon (IC), total organic carbon (TOC) and non-purgeable organic carbon (NPOC); an optional accessory enables the measurement of particulate organic carbon (POC) and total nitrogen (TN) as well. The instrument uses the 680 degC combustion catalytic oxidation method to analyse aqueous samples, and optionally solid and gas samples. TOC-VCPH analyses sample injection volumes within (10 - 2000) uL, and the measurement ranges are (0-25) g/L for TC, and (0-30) g/L for IC; the detection limit is 4 ug/L, and the coefficient of variation is at most 1.5%. The optional TN accessory measures within the (0-4) g/L range, at a detection limit of 5 ug/L and with a coefficient of variation of at most 3%."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL0849";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Shimadzu Total Organic Carbon Analyser (TOC-VCPH)"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00919/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1400/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL1400";
        dc:date                "2020-02-12 16:42:36.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL1400";
        pav:authoredOn         "2020-02-12 16:42:36.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL1400/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "VMCM2";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/114/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/385/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/134/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/>;
        skos:definition        "The VMCM2 current meter is based on the original VMCM instrument. The original rotors and housing hardware are retained; only the internal chassis and electronics are replaced. The VMCM has two orthogonal cosine response propeller sensors that measure the components of horizontal current velocity parallel to the axles of the two-propeller sensors. The orientation of the instrument relative to magnetic north is determined by a flux gate compass. East and north components of velocity are computed continuously, averaged and then stored on flash memory. Temperature is also recorded using a thermistor mounted in a fast response pod, mounted on the top end cap of the VMCM. The VMCM2 Current Meter is based on the original VMCM instrument. The original rotors, \"sting\", and housing hardware are retained; only the internal chassis and electronics are replaced."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL1400";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Woods Hole Oceanographic Institution VMCM 2 {ng-vmcm} (submersible) vector measuring current meter"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0064/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00135/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0868/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL0868";
        dc:date                "2024-07-22 10:12:39.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL0868";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-07-22 10:12:39.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0868/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0868/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "SV Plus";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/185/>;
        skos:definition        "An instrument that measures the velocity of sound in seawater and can assist creating profiles for input into echosounders to correct the varying passage of sound waves through the water column. The SV Plus was the pre-2002 predecesssor to the SV Plus V2. Applied Microsystems Ltd., is also known as AML Oceanographic."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL0868";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Applied Microsystems Ltd SV Plus probe"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG0236/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2204/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL2204";
        dc:date                "2025-08-13 16:18:01.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL2204";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-08-13 16:18:01.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2204/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Burns CR-100-27";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/369/>;
        skos:definition        "The CR-100-27 is an encapsulated active ceramic hydrophone, featuring a sound-transparent rubber encapsulant. This provides high sensitivity and wide band (between 7 and 100 kHz) frequency range. The hydrophone also features an ultra-low noise, high impedance 27 dB field-effect transistor (FET) preamplifier to provide signal conditioning. The hydrophone has both scientific and commercial applications in cetacean research/monitoring, and underwater filming. Ceramic resonant frequency is > 200 kHz. Typical sensitivity is -179 dB +/- 5 dB. Operating depth is up to 400 metres, and operating temperature range is -1 to 55 degC. The hydrophone is omnidirectional when deployed horizontally (+/- 3 dB at 1 kHz), and 260 degrees when deployed vertically (+/- 6 dB at 1 kHz)."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL2204";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Burns Electronics CR-100-27 hydrophone"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0354/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG02126/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0887/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL0887";
        dc:date                "2015-06-18 13:58:38.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL0887";
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-06-18 13:58:38.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0887/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Aquadopp 600 kHz profiler";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0888/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/134/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/115/>;
        skos:definition        "A self-contained 600 kHz Doppler current profiler designed for deployment on the seabed, moorings, buoys or fixed structures. The instrument uses 3 beams to measure water velocities over a range of +/-10 m/s and has a standard depth rating of 300 m with 3000 m or 600m versions available. Range is 30-40m. Depth cell size ranges from 1-4 m, with a maximum of 128 cells. Temperature (embedded thermistor with 0.1C accuracy and 0.01C resolution), compass (magnetometer with 2 degrees accuracy and 0.1 degree resolution providing tilt <20 degrees), tilt (liquid level with 0.2 degree accuracy and 0.1 degree resolution) and pressure (piezo resistive with accuracy of 0.5% full scale - usually 100m - and resolution of 0.005% full scale) sensors are provided as standard."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL0887";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Nortek Aquadopp 600 kHz Doppler current profiler"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00333/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2223/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL2223";
        dc:date                "2025-10-03 12:59:24.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL2223";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-10-03 12:59:24.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2223/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "EnvLogger T7.3";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/134/>;
        skos:definition        "The EnvLogger T7.3 is a customisable temperature sensor suitable for deployment in harsh aquatic and terrestrial environments. It can operate within a temperature range of -30 to 60 degC and can be deployed at depths of down to 4000 m. The logger comes in a standard 29 mm resin disc or can be encapsulated in biomimetic casings. The battery has a minimum lifespan of approximately 15 years at a 1 per hour sample rate (at 20 degC). The logger can record at a resolution of 0.1 or 0.5 degC. Data from the logger are transferred to a smartphone via the EnvLogger Viewer software using wireless Near Field Communication (NFC) technology."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL2223";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ElectricBlue EnvLogger T7.3 temperature sensor"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0363/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG02134/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2242/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL2242";
        dc:date                "2025-11-21 16:11:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL2242";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-11-21 16:11:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2242/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Insite Pacific Aurora Plus";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/311/>;
        skos:definition        "A miniature colour CCD video camera, ideal for applications including surveillance, inspection ROV, and remote tooling systems. The camera has a fixed focus, wide angle lens and requires no external controls in normal operation. Video output: Composite 1Vpp. The Aurora Plus has a high resolution, low light, colour CCD sensor within a compact titanium pressure housing. Lens: 3.6 mm, F2.0; Focus Range: 8 inches to infinity; Field of View: 73 degrees diagonal, 61 degrees horizontal; 48 degrees vertical. Storage temperature: -10 to 50 degrees C. Operating temperature: -20 to 60 degrees C. Optional pressure housings up to 13 km depth rating are available."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL2242";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Insite Pacific Aurora Plus miniature colour camera"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0255/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG02006/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2280/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL2280";
        dc:date                "2026-03-13 15:30:52.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL2280";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-03-13 15:30:52.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2280/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "LISST-Tau";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/124/>;
        skos:definition        "The Sequoia Laser In-Situ Scattering and Transmissometry (LISST)-Tau is a transmissometer suitable for use on underwater vehicles, profiling packages, CTDs, and other systems. It measures optical transmission and beam attenuation. The LISST-Tau transmits a collimated beam through the water and measures the light transmitted through its 15 cm path. Light modulation with synchronous detection rejects ambient light, while oversampling and averaging yield better than 16-bit resolution. LISST-Tau's digital controller applies calibration coefficients, corrects for temperature effects, and transmits data from both digital and analog outputs. Included software provides real-time display of data, and functions for checking and updating pure-water calibrations. Optical path length: 15 cm; source wavelength: ~532 nm (green) or ~ 650 nm (red) LED; source spectral bandwidth: <10 nm Full Width at Half Maximum; acceptance angle (half angle, in water): 1 degree. An optional flow-through chamber is available for use. Operating temperature range: -3 to 40 degC; storage temperature range: -20 to 60 degC; beam attenuation range: ~0 to 30 m^-1; linearity (concentration): >99 percent. Depth rating to 2000 m; sampling rate: 1 Hz."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL2280";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Sequoia LISST-Tau transmissometer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00275/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0057/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0608/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL0608";
        dc:date                "2013-03-22 16:42:24.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL0608";
        pav:authoredOn         "2013-03-22 16:42:24.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0608/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Eliasson CBME80 cloud ceilometer";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L19/current/SDNKG17/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/CCOV/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/ATRANS/>;
        skos:definition        "An infrared laser diode measuring the cloud base height or vertical visibility and cloud amount. The design is based on the LIDAR principle. The light emitting component is a low power diode laser with the output power limited to eye-safe level. Real time digitising technique is used in signal detection and the 80C186 microprocessor is used in signal processing."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL0608";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Eliasson CBME80 infrared laser diode cloud ceilometer"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG00716/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2307/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL2307";
        dc:date                "2026-05-28 16:13:26.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:L22::TOOL2307";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-05-28 16:13:26.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2307/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Insite Pacific Mini Zeus MKIII";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L05/current/311/>;
        skos:definition        "A high definition (HD) 1080p / 1080i complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor (CMOS) colour zoom video camera. The High-definition television (HDTV) camera provides 2,130,000 pixels compared to roughly 410,000 from standard definition cameras. The camera can be provided in a housing rated from 1000 to 7500 metres depth. A glass hemispherical viewport and Insite Pacific's exclusive fully underwater corrected optical lens system corrects for chromatic and geometric distortion, astigmatism, and other optical abnormalities including eliminating zoom and focus tracking errors. The Mark III features HD-SCI and 3G-SDI outputs of 1080p/60, 1080p/59.94, 1080p/50, 1080p/29.97, 1080p/25, 1080i/60, 1080i/59.94, 1080i/50, 720p/59.94, 720p/50, 720p/29.97, and 720p/25. Focus, iris, and zoom can be controlled via DC voltages, a GUI, or Insite Pacific's Camera/Lens Controller. An optional 2.97 Gb/s 3D-SDI video converter mounted inside the pressure housing with a fibre optic connector can provide transmission of the video signal for distances of up to 30 km. Operating temperature from -5 to +50 degC. Focus range at full telephoto: 8 inches (203 mm) to infinity. Focus range at full wide: front of dome to infinity. Iris range: F1.6 to Closed. The camera features a 30x 4.3 - 129 mm wide angle or telephoto lens, with 139.4 or 6.8 degrees (diagonal), 134 or 6.4 degrees (horizontal) and 105.9 or 3.6 degrees (vertical) angles of view respectively."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/SDNDEV/current/>;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L22::TOOL2307";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "Insite Pacific Mini Zeus Mark III camera"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L35/current/MAN0255/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B75/current/ORG02006/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL0646/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:L22::TOOL0646";
        dc:date                "2013-09-30 14:19:16.0";
